Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Common non-office email-attachment file-type associations for the em Client
; CrossOver/Wine bottle -- images, archives, audio, video, plus a couple of text
; formats (.json, .md) that turned up missing too.
;
; Found the same way as file-associations/office-associations.reg was: em Client's
; own file-open logic (MailClient.UI.ShellInterop.OpenItem / OpenFileInDefaultApp,
; see reports/office-file-associations-findings.md) only has special internal
; handling for .eml/.msg/.emlt/.oft/.vcf/.ics/.asc/.crt/.cer/.note/.pst/.emdf --
; every other attachment type, these included, falls through to the OS file
; association exactly like .docx did, so any extension with no working association
; hits the same Wine shell32 "There is no Windows program configured to open this
; type of file." message.
;
; Checked against a fresh emClient_win_8_x64 bottle's registry: .jpg/.jpeg, .png,
; .gif, .txt, .htm/.html and .xml already had working associations out of the box
; and are deliberately NOT touched here. Everything below was either missing the
; extension key entirely, present with an empty default value (no ProgID), or --
; .svg specifically -- pointing at a ProgID ("svgfile") that doesn't itself exist,
; so .svg's entry below overwrites that dangling default rather than adding a new
; one (note: this means a plain "does the extension already have a value" merge
; check, as used by deploy.sh's selective-import logic, will treat .svg as already
; associated and skip it -- --force-associations is needed to actually fix .svg).
;
; Same ProgID scheme and same winebrowser.exe handler as office-associations.reg --
; see that file's own header comment for the reasoning (avoids colliding with any
; real app's ProgID, delegates to the host's own xdg-open MIME resolution).

; --- Images ---
[HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT\.bmp]
@="EMClientWinePort.bmp"

[HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT\EMClientWinePort.bmp\shell\open\command]
@="\"c:\\windows\\system32\\winebrowser.exe\" \"%1\""

[HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT\.tif]
@="EMClientWinePort.tif"

[HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT\EMClientWinePort.tif\shell\open\command]
@="\"c:\\windows\\system32\\winebrowser.exe\" \"%1\""

